      <section class="workflow"><div class="shell"><p class="kicker">Development workflow</p><h2>From platform requirements to a reusable lab instrument</h2><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><h3>Map research needs</h3><p>Defined vehicle, display, ADAS, input, data, and monitoring requirements around future experimental use.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Redesign the architecture</h3><p>Separated programs and standardized topic-based state exchange through MQTT and JSON messages.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Prototype multiple surfaces</h3><p>Connected instrument, center-display, HUD, secondary-vehicle, and monitoring experiences to shared states.</p></li><li><span>04</span><h3>Integrate physical controls</h3><p>Mapped the steering wheel, pedals, and buttons to manual driving, automated functions, and experiment inputs.</p></li><li><span>05</span><h3>Operationalize for studies</h3><p>Iterated scenarios, display states, data visibility, and test procedures until other projects could reuse the system.</p></li></ol></div></section>

